    'Determining the number of columns required' => 'Menentukan jumlah kolom yang diperlukan',
    'When you perform a SQL injection UNION attack, there are two effective methods to determine how many columns are being returned from the original query.' => 'Saat melakukan serangan SQL injection UNION, terdapat dua metode efektif untuk mengetahui jumlah kolom kueri asal.',
    'One method involves injecting a series of [[C0]] clauses and incrementing the specified column index until an error occurs. For example, if the injection point is a quoted string within the [[C1]] clause of the original query, you would submit:' => 'Metode pertama menyisipkan rangkaian klausa [[C0]] dengan indeks kolom yang terus dinaikkan sampai error muncul. Misalnya, jika titik injeksi berada di dalam string berkutip pada klausa [[C1]], Anda bisa mengirim:',
    'This series of payloads modifies the original query to order the results by different columns in the result set. The column in an [[C0]] clause can be specified by its index, so you don\'t need to know the names of any columns. When the specified column index exceeds the number of actual columns in the result set, the database returns an error, such as:' => 'Rangkaian payload ini mengurutkan hasil berdasarkan nomor indeks kolom, sehingga Anda tidak perlu mengetahui nama kolom aslinya. Ketika indeks melebihi jumlah kolom yang tersedia, database akan memunculkan error seperti:',
    'The application might actually return the database error in its HTTP response, but it may also issue a generic error response. In other cases, it may simply return no results at all. Either way, as long as you can detect some difference in the response, you can infer how many columns are being returned from the query.' => 'Aplikasi bisa saja menampilkan pesan error database di respons HTTP, menampilkan pesan error umum, atau sekadar mengembalikan hasil kosong. Selama perbedaan respons tersebut bisa diamati, Anda tetap dapat menyimpulkan jumlah kolom kueri asal.',
    'The second method involves submitting a series of [[C0]] payloads specifying a different number of null values:' => 'Metode kedua mengirimkan rangkaian payload [[C0]] dengan jumlah nilai null yang terus bertambah:',
    'If the number of nulls does not match the number of columns, the database returns an error, such as:' => 'Jika jumlah null belum sesuai dengan jumlah kolom, database akan memunculkan error seperti:',
    'We use [[C0]] as the values returned from the injected [[C1]] query because the data types in each column must be compatible between the original and the injected queries. [[C2]] is convertible to every common data type, so it maximizes the chance that the payload will succeed when the column count is correct.' => 'Nilai [[C0]] dipilih pada kueri [[C1]] sisipan karena tipe data tiap kolom harus kompatibel dengan kueri asal. [[C2]] cocok dengan hampir semua tipe data umum, sehingga peluang berhasilnya jauh lebih tinggi begitu jumlah kolomnya tepat.',
    'As with the [[C0]] technique, the application might actually return the database error in its HTTP response, but may return a generic error or simply return no results. When the number of nulls matches the number of columns, the database returns an additional row in the result set, containing null values in each column. The effect on the HTTP response depends on the application\'s code. If you are lucky, you will see some additional content within the response, such as an extra row on an HTML table. Otherwise, the null values might trigger a different error, such as a [[C1]]. In the worst case, the response might look the same as a response caused by an incorrect number of nulls. This would make this method ineffective.' => 'Seperti halnya metode [[C0]], respons error bisa tampil rinci, bersifat umum, atau menghasilkan daftar kosong. Ketika jumlah null cocok dengan jumlah kolom, database menambahkan satu baris berisi nilai null. Dampaknya di respons HTTP bergantung pada kode aplikasi: kadang muncul baris ekstra pada tabel HTML, atau memicu error berbeda seperti [[C1]]. Pada kasus paling sulit, responsnya tampak sama persis dengan jumlah null yang salah sehingga metode ini tidak efektif.',
    'Database-specific syntax' => 'Sintaks khusus per database',
    'On Oracle, every [[C0]] query must use the [[C1]] keyword and specify a valid table. There is a built-in table on Oracle called [[C2]] which can be used for this purpose. So the injected queries on Oracle would need to look like:' => 'Di Oracle, setiap kueri [[C0]] wajib menyertakan kata kunci [[C1]] dan nama tabel yang valid. Oracle memiliki tabel bawaan bernama [[C2]] yang bisa dipakai untuk keperluan ini, sehingga payload pada Oracle berbentuk:',
    'The payloads described use the double-dash comment sequence [[C0]] to comment out the remainder of the original query following the injection point. On MySQL, the double-dash sequence must be followed by a space. Alternatively, the hash character [[C1]] can be used to identify a comment.' => 'Contoh payload di atas memakai dua tanda hubung [[C0]] untuk mengomentari sisa kueri setelah titik injeksi. Di MySQL, penanda tersebut harus diikuti spasi, atau sebagai alternatif gunakan karakter pagar [[C1]].',
    'For more details of database-specific syntax, see the [[A0]]SQL injection cheat sheet[[/A0]].' => 'Untuk rincian sintaks tiap jenis database, lihat [[A0]]contekan SQL injection[[/A0]].',
    'Finding columns with a useful data type' => 'Mencari kolom dengan tipe data yang berguna',
    'A SQL injection UNION attack enables you to retrieve the results from an injected query. The interesting data that you want to retrieve is normally in string form. This means you need to find one or more columns in the original query results whose data type is, or is compatible with, string data.' => 'Serangan SQL injection UNION memungkinkan penguji mengambil hasil dari kueri sisipan. Karena data target umumnya berupa string, Anda perlu menemukan kolom dari kueri asal yang bertipe string atau kompatibel dengannya.',
    'After you determine the number of required columns, you can probe each column to test whether it can hold string data. You can submit a series of [[C0]] payloads that place a string value into each column in turn. For example, if the query returns four columns, you would submit:' => 'Setelah jumlah kolom diketahui, uji tiap posisi kolom secara bergiliran dengan mengisi nilai string melalui payload [[C0]]. Misalnya jika terdapat empat kolom, kirimkan:',
    'If the column data type is not compatible with string data, the injected query will cause a database error, such as:' => 'Jika kolom tidak kompatibel dengan data string, kueri sisipan akan menimbulkan error database seperti:',
    'If an error does not occur, and the application\'s response contains some additional content including the injected string value, then the relevant column is suitable for retrieving string data.' => 'Jika tidak terjadi error dan respons aplikasi menampilkan teks string yang Anda sisipkan, berarti kolom tersebut siap dipakai untuk menarik data string.',
    'Using a SQL injection UNION attack to retrieve interesting data' => 'Menggunakan serangan SQL injection UNION untuk mengambil data penting',
    'When you have determined the number of columns returned by the original query and found which columns can hold string data, you are in a position to retrieve interesting data.' => 'Begitu jumlah kolom dan posisi kolom bertipe string sudah ditemukan, Anda siap mengambil data yang diincar.',
    'Suppose that:' => 'Misalkan skenarionya seperti ini:',
    'The original query returns two columns, both of which can hold string data.' => 'Kueri asal mengembalikan dua kolom yang sama-sama menampung data string.',
    'The injection point is a quoted string within the [[C0]] clause.' => 'Titik injeksi berada di dalam string berkutip pada klausa [[C0]].',
    'The database contains a table called [[C0]] with the columns [[C1]] and [[C2]].' => 'Database memiliki tabel bernama [[C0]] dengan kolom [[C1]] dan [[C2]].',
    'In this example, you can retrieve the contents of the [[C0]] table by submitting the input:' => 'Pada contoh ini, isi tabel [[C0]] dapat diambil dengan mengirimkan input:',
    'In order to perform this attack, you need to know that there is a table called [[C0]] with two columns called [[C1]] and [[C2]]. Without this information, you would have to guess the names of the tables and columns. All modern databases provide ways to examine the database structure, and determine what tables and columns they contain.' => 'Untuk menjalankan serangan ini, Anda perlu mengetahui keberadaan tabel [[C0]] serta nama kolom [[C1]] dan [[C2]]. Tanpa informasi tersebut, Anda hanya bisa menebak. Untungnya, semua database modern menyediakan mekanisme untuk melihat struktur tabel dan kolom di dalamnya.',
    'Retrieving multiple values within a single column' => 'Mengambil beberapa nilai dalam satu kolom',
    'In some cases the query in the previous example may only return a single column.' => 'Dalam beberapa situasi, kueri asal pada contoh sebelumnya mungkin hanya mengembalikan satu kolom.',
    'You can retrieve multiple values together within this single column by concatenating the values together. You can include a separator to let you distinguish the combined values. For example, on Oracle you could submit the input:' => 'Anda tetap bisa menarik beberapa nilai sekaligus di satu kolom tersebut dengan menggabungkannya disertai karakter pemisah agar mudah dibedakan. Contohnya di Oracle:',
    'This uses the double-pipe sequence [[C0]] which is a string concatenation operator on Oracle. The injected query concatenates together the values of the [[C1]] and [[C2]] fields, separated by the [[C3]] character.' => 'Payload di atas menggunakan operator pipa ganda [[C0]] untuk penggabungan string di Oracle, menggabungkan kolom [[C1]] dan [[C2]] yang dipisahkan oleh karakter [[C3]].',
    'The results from the query contain all the usernames and passwords, for example:' => 'Hasil kueri kemudian akan menampilkan seluruh pasangan username dan kata sandi, misalnya:',
    'Different databases use different syntax to perform string concatenation. For more details, see the [[A0]]SQL injection cheat sheet[[/A0]].' => 'Setiap sistem database menggunakan sintaks penggabungan string yang berbeda. Lihat [[A0]]contekan SQL injection[[/A0]] untuk detail tiap platform.',

    // examining-the-database
    'To exploit SQL injection vulnerabilities, it\'s often necessary to find information about the database. This includes:' => 'Untuk mengeksploitasi celah SQL injection secara efektif, penguji kerap perlu mengumpulkan informasi struktur database, mencakup:',
    'The type and version of the database software.' => 'Jenis dan versi perangkat lunak database.',
    'The tables and columns that the database contains.' => 'Daftar tabel dan kolom yang ada di dalam database.',
    'Querying the database type and version' => 'Menanyakan tipe dan versi database',
    'You can potentially identify both the database type and version by injecting provider-specific queries to see if one works' => 'Anda dapat mengidentifikasi jenis sekaligus versi database dengan mencoba kueri khas masing-masing vendor untuk melihat mana yang berhasil dijalankan.',
    'The following are some queries to determine the database version for some popular database types:' => 'Berikut beberapa contoh kueri untuk mengetahui versi pada jenis database yang umum digunakan:',
    'Database type' => 'Jenis database',
    'Query' => 'Kueri',
    'Microsoft, MySQL' => 'Microsoft, MySQL',
    'For example, you could use a [[C0]] attack with the following input:' => 'Misalnya, Anda dapat melakukan serangan [[C0]] memakai input berikut:',
    'This might return the following output. In this case, you can confirm that the database is Microsoft SQL Server and see the version used:' => 'Output yang kembali bisa tampak seperti berikut, yang memastikan database berjalan di Microsoft SQL Server beserta versinya:',
    'Listing the contents of the database' => 'Melihat daftar isi database',
    'Most database types (except Oracle) have a set of views called the information schema. This provides information about the database.' => 'Mayoritas jenis database (kecuali Oracle) memiliki sekumpulan view bernama information schema yang menyimpan metadata struktur database.',
    'For example, you can query [[C0]] to list the tables in the database:' => 'Misalnya, Anda bisa mengueri [[C0]] untuk melihat seluruh tabel yang ada:',
    'This returns output like the following:' => 'Hasilnya tampak seperti berikut:',
    'This output indicates that there are three tables, called [[C0]], [[C1]], and [[C2]].' => 'Output tersebut menunjukkan adanya tiga tabel bernama [[C0]], [[C1]], dan [[C2]].',
    'You can then query [[C0]] to list the columns in individual tables:' => 'Setelah itu, kueri [[C0]] untuk melihat daftar kolom di tabel tertentu:',
    'This output shows the columns in the specified table and the data type of each column.' => 'Output ini menampilkan nama kolom pada tabel yang dipilih beserta tipe datanya.',
    'Listing the contents of an Oracle database' => 'Melihat daftar isi database Oracle',
    'On Oracle, you can find the same information as follows:' => 'Di Oracle, informasi yang sama dapat ditemukan dengan cara berikut:',
    'You can list tables by querying [[C0]]:' => 'Daftar tabel dapat diperoleh dengan mengueri [[C0]]:',
    'You can list columns by querying [[C0]]:' => 'Daftar kolom dapat diperoleh dengan mengueri [[C0]]:',

    // blind
    'In this section, we describe techniques for finding and exploiting blind SQL injection vulnerabilities.' => 'Di bagian ini dibahas teknik untuk menemukan dan mengeksploitasi kerentanan blind SQL injection.',
    'What is blind SQL injection?' => 'Apa itu blind SQL injection?',
    'Blind SQL injection occurs when an application is vulnerable to SQL injection, but its HTTP responses do not contain the results of the relevant SQL query or the details of any database errors.' => 'Blind SQL injection terjadi ketika aplikasi rentan terhadap SQL injection, tetapi respons HTTP-nya tidak memuat hasil kueri SQL maupun detail pesan error database.',
    'Many techniques such as [[A0]][[C0]] attacks[[/A0]] are not effective with blind SQL injection vulnerabilities. This is because they rely on being able to see the results of the injected query within the application\'s responses. It is still possible to exploit blind SQL injection to access unauthorized data, but different techniques must be used.' => 'Banyak teknik seperti serangan [[A0]][[C0]][[/A0]] tidak berjalan pada blind SQL injection karena bergantung pada tampaknya hasil kueri di respons. Pengambilalihan data secara ilegal tetap bisa dilakukan, namun memakai pendekatan berbeda.',
    'Exploiting blind SQL injection by triggering conditional responses' => 'Mengeksploitasi blind SQL injection dengan memicu respons bersyarat',
    'Consider an application that uses tracking cookies to gather analytics about usage. Requests to the application include a cookie header like this:' => 'Perhatikan contoh aplikasi yang memakai tracking cookie untuk mencatat analitik penggunaan. Setiap permintaan membawa header cookie seperti berikut:',
    'When a request containing a [[C0]] cookie is processed, the application uses a SQL query to determine whether this is a known user:' => 'Saat permintaan berisi cookie [[C0]] diterima, aplikasi menjalankan kueri SQL untuk mengecek apakah pengguna sudah dikenali:',
    'This query is vulnerable to SQL injection, but the results from the query are not returned to the user. However, the application does behave differently depending on whether the query returns any data. If you submit a recognized [[C0]], the query returns data and you receive a "Welcome back" message in the response.' => 'Kueri tersebut rentan terhadap SQL injection meski hasilnya tidak dikirim balik ke pengguna. Namun perilaku respons aplikasi berubah bergantung pada ada tidaknya data yang cocok: saat [[C0]] valid, kueri mengembalikan baris data dan respons menampilkan pesan "Welcome back".',
    'This behavior is enough to be able to exploit the blind SQL injection vulnerability. You can retrieve information by triggering different responses conditionally, depending on an injected condition.' => 'Perbedaan perilaku sekecil ini sudah cukup untuk mengeksploitasi celah blind SQL injection dengan memicu respons berbeda berdasarkan kondisi logika yang disisipkan.',
    'To understand how this exploit works, suppose that two requests are sent containing the following [[C0]] cookie values in turn:' => 'Untuk memahami mekanismenya, misalkan dua permintaan dikirim bergantian dengan nilai cookie [[C0]] berikut:',
    'The first of these values causes the query to return results, because the injected [[C0]] condition is true. As a result, the "Welcome back" message is displayed.' => 'Nilai pertama membuat kueri mengembalikan hasil karena kondisi sisipan [[C0]] bernilai benar, sehingga pesan "Welcome back" muncul.',
    'The second value causes the query to not return any results, because the injected condition is false. The "Welcome back" message is not displayed.' => 'Nilai kedua membuat kueri tidak mengembalikan baris karena kondisinya salah, sehingga pesan "Welcome back" tidak tampil.',
    'This allows us to determine the answer to any single injected condition, and extract data one piece at a time.' => 'Dengan pola ini, kita dapat mengetahui jawaban benar atau salah dari kondisi apa pun dan menarik data sedikit demi sedikit.',
    'For example, suppose there is a table called [[C0]] with the columns [[C1]] and [[C2]], and a user called [[C3]]. You can determine the password for this user by sending a series of inputs to test the password one character at a time.' => 'Misalnya ada tabel [[C0]] dengan kolom [[C1]] dan [[C2]] serta akun [[C3]]. Kata sandi akun tersebut dapat ditebak karakter demi karakter melalui serangkaian input uji.',
    'To do this, start with the following input:' => 'Mulailah dengan mengirim input seperti berikut:',
    'This returns the "Welcome back" message, indicating that the injected condition is true, and so the first character of the password is greater than [[C0]].' => 'Respons memunculkan pesan "Welcome back", menandakan kondisi benar dan huruf pertama kata sandi berada di atas [[C0]].',
    'Next, we send the following input:' => 'Berikutnya, kirim input uji lanjutan:',
    'This does not return the "Welcome back" message, indicating that the injected condition is false, and so the first character of the password is not greater than [[C0]].' => 'Pesan "Welcome back" tidak muncul, berarti kondisi salah dan huruf pertama kata sandi tidak lebih besar dari [[C0]].',
    'Eventually, we send the following input, which returns the "Welcome back" message, thereby confirming that the first character of the password is [[C0]]:' => 'Hingga akhirnya input berikut mengembalikan pesan "Welcome back", yang memastikan huruf pertama kata sandi adalah [[C0]]:',
    'We can continue this process to systematically determine the full password for the [[C0]] user.' => 'Proses ini dilanjutkan secara sistematis sampai seluruh karakter kata sandi [[C0]] berhasil ditemukan.',
    'The [[C0]] function is called [[C1]] on some types of database. For more details, see the [[A0]]SQL injection cheat sheet[[/A0]].' => 'Pada beberapa jenis database, fungsi [[C0]] bernama [[C1]]. Lihat [[A0]]contekan SQL injection[[/A0]] untuk detailnya.',
    'Error-based SQL injection refers to cases where you\'re able to use error messages to either extract or infer sensitive data from the database, even in blind contexts. The possibilities depend on the configuration of the database and the types of errors you\'re able to trigger:' => 'Error-based SQL injection memanfaatkan pesan error database untuk mengekstrak atau menyimpulkan data sensitif, bahkan pada skenario blind. Teknik yang berhasil bergantung pada konfigurasi database serta jenis error yang bisa dipicu:',
    'You may be able to induce the application to return a specific error response based on the result of a boolean expression. You can exploit this in the same way as the [[A0]]conditional responses[[/A0]] we looked at in the previous section. For more information, see [[A1]]Exploiting blind SQL injection by triggering conditional errors[[/A1]].' => 'Memancing aplikasi agar mengembalikan respons error tertentu saat kondisi boolean terpenuhi. Prinsipnya sama dengan [[A0]]respons bersyarat[[/A0]] di bagian sebelumnya. Lihat [[A1]]Eksploitasi blind SQL injection lewat error bersyarat[[/A1]].',
    'You may be able to trigger error messages that output the data returned by the query. This effectively turns otherwise blind SQL injection vulnerabilities into visible ones. For more information, see [[A0]]Extracting sensitive data via verbose SQL error messages[[/A0]].' => 'Memicu pesan error yang sekaligus membocorkan hasil kueri, sehingga celah blind berubah menjadi error terlihat. Lihat [[A0]]Mengekstrak data lewat pesan error SQL rinci[[/A0]].',
    'Exploiting blind SQL injection by triggering conditional errors' => 'Mengeksploitasi blind SQL injection dengan memicu error bersyarat',
    'Some applications carry out SQL queries but their behavior doesn\'t change, regardless of whether the query returns any data. The technique in the previous section won\'t work, because injecting different boolean conditions makes no difference to the application\'s responses.' => 'Ada kalanya aplikasi menjalankan kueri SQL tetapi perilaku responsnya sama sekali tidak berubah, ada atau tidaknya data yang kembali. Teknik sebelumnya tidak mempan karena perbedaan kondisi boolean tidak mengubah isi halaman.',
    'It\'s often possible to induce the application to return a different response depending on whether a SQL error occurs. You can modify the query so that it causes a database error only if the condition is true. Very often, an unhandled error thrown by the database causes some difference in the application\'s response, such as an error message. This enables you to infer the truth of the injected condition.' => 'Dalam situasi itu, Anda sering masih bisa memicu respons berbeda berdasarkan terjadi tidaknya error SQL. Kueri dimodifikasi agar memunculkan error hanya bila kondisi tertentu bernilai benar. Error database yang tidak tertangani biasanya mengubah respons HTTP sehingga kebenaran kondisi tetap dapat disimpulkan.',
    'To see how this works, suppose that two requests are sent containing the following [[C0]] cookie values in turn:' => 'Sebagai gambaran, misalkan dua permintaan dikirim berturut-turut dengan nilai cookie [[C0]] seperti ini:',
    'These inputs use the [[C0]] keyword to test a condition and return a different expression depending on whether the expression is true:' => 'Kedua input memanfaatkan kata kunci [[C0]] untuk mengevaluasi kondisi dan memilih ekspresi berbeda berdasarkan hasilnya:',
    'With the first input, the [[C0]] expression evaluates to [[C1]], which does not cause any error.' => 'Pada input pertama, ekspresi [[C0]] menghasilkan [[C1]] sehingga tidak menimbulkan error.',
    'With the second input, it evaluates to [[C0]], which causes a divide-by-zero error.' => 'Pada input kedua, ekspresi bernilai [[C0]] yang langsung memicu error pembagian dengan nol.',
    'If the error causes a difference in the application\'s HTTP response, you can use this to determine whether the injected condition is true.' => 'Jika error tersebut memunculkan perbedaan pada respons HTTP, Anda dapat memakainya untuk menentukan benar tidaknya kondisi yang disisipkan.',
    'Using this technique, you can retrieve data by testing one character at a time:' => 'Dengan teknik yang sama, data dapat diekstrak satu karakter demi satu karakter:',
    'There are different ways of triggering conditional errors, and different techniques work best on different database types. For more details, see the [[A0]]SQL injection cheat sheet[[/A0]].' => 'Ada berbagai cara memicu error bersyarat, dan masing-masing jenis database memakai sintaks terbaiknya sendiri. Lihat [[A0]]contekan SQL injection[[/A0]] untuk daftar lengkapnya.',
    'Extracting sensitive data via verbose SQL error messages' => 'Mengekstrak data sensitif lewat pesan error SQL rinci',
    'Misconfiguration of the database sometimes results in verbose error messages. These can provide information that may be useful to an attacker. For example, consider the following error message, which occurs after injecting a single quote into an [[C0]] parameter:' => 'Salah konfigurasi database terkadang memunculkan pesan error terperinci yang membantu penyerang. Contohnya pesan error berikut yang muncul setelah menyisipkan kutip tunggal pada parameter [[C0]]:',
    'This shows the full query that the application constructed using our input. We can see that in this case, we\'re injecting into a single-quoted string inside a [[C0]] statement. This makes it easier to construct a valid query containing a malicious payload. Commenting out the rest of the query would prevent the superfluous single-quote from breaking the syntax.' => 'Pesan tersebut memperlihatkan utuh struktur kueri yang dirangkai aplikasi, termasuk bahwa input berada di dalam string kutip tunggal pada klausa [[C0]]. Dari situ penyerang mudah meracik payload valid sambil mengomentari sisa kueri agar tanda kutip tambahan tidak merusak sintaks.',
    'Occasionally, you may be able to induce the application to generate an error message that contains some of the data that is returned by the query. This effectively turns an otherwise blind SQL injection vulnerability into a visible one.' => 'Terkadang aplikasi dapat dipaksa memunculkan pesan error yang memuat hasil kueri secara langsung, mengubah celah blind menjadi terlihat.',
    'You can use the [[C0]] function to achieve this. It enables you to convert one data type to another. For example, imagine a query containing the following statement:' => 'Fungsi [[C0]] dapat dipakai untuk mengonversi satu tipe data ke tipe lain demi memicu error semacam itu, misalnya pada pernyataan berikut:',
    'Often, the data that you\'re trying to read is a string. Attempting to convert this to an incompatible data type, such as an [[C0]], may cause an error similar to the following:' => 'Karena data yang dicari umumnya berupa string, percobaan mengonversinya menjadi tipe tidak cocok seperti [[C0]] dapat menghasilkan error seperti berikut:',
    'This type of query may also be useful if a character limit prevents you from triggering conditional responses.' => 'Pendekatan ini juga sangat berguna apabila batas panjang karakter tidak memungkinkan penggunaan teknik respons bersyarat.',
    'Exploiting blind SQL injection by triggering time delays' => 'Mengeksploitasi blind SQL injection dengan memicu jeda waktu',
    'If the application catches database errors when the SQL query is executed and handles them gracefully, there won\'t be any difference in the application\'s response. This means the previous technique for inducing conditional errors will not work.' => 'Apabila aplikasi menangkap setiap error database dan menanganinya dengan rapi, respons HTTP tidak akan menunjukkan perbedaan sehingga teknik error bersyarat tidak dapat digunakan.',
    'In this situation, it is often possible to exploit the blind SQL injection vulnerability by triggering time delays depending on whether an injected condition is true or false. As SQL queries are normally processed synchronously by the application, delaying the execution of a SQL query also delays the HTTP response. This allows you to determine the truth of the injected condition based on the time taken to receive the HTTP response.' => 'Pada kondisi seperti itu, celah blind SQL injection tetap dapat dieksploitasi lewat jeda waktu eksekusi kueri yang dipicu secara bersyarat. Karena kueri SQL umumnya diproses secara sinkron, perlambatan kueri ikut menunda respons HTTP sehingga kebenaran kondisi dapat diketahui dari waktu responnya.',
    'The techniques for triggering a time delay are specific to the type of database being used. For example, on Microsoft SQL Server, you can use the following to test a condition and trigger a delay depending on whether the expression is true:' => 'Perintah jeda waktu bergantung pada jenis database target. Pada Microsoft SQL Server misalnya, Anda bisa menguji kondisi dan memicu jeda lewat payload berikut:',
    'The first of these inputs does not trigger a delay, because the condition [[C0]] is false.' => 'Input pertama tidak memicu jeda karena kondisi [[C0]] bernilai salah.',
    'The second input triggers a delay of 10 seconds, because the condition [[C0]] is true.' => 'Input kedua memicu jeda 10 detik karena kondisi [[C0]] bernilai benar.',
    'Using this technique, we can retrieve data by testing one character at a time:' => 'Memakai teknik ini, data dapat ditarik satu karakter demi satu karakter:',
    'There are various ways to trigger time delays within SQL queries, and different techniques apply on different types of database. For more details, see the [[A0]]SQL injection cheat sheet[[/A0]].' => 'Ada beragam sintaks untuk memicu jeda waktu pada kueri SQL sesuai jenis databasenya. Lihat [[A0]]contekan SQL injection[[/A0]] untuk rincian lengkap.',
    'Exploiting blind SQL injection using out-of-band (OAST) techniques' => 'Mengeksploitasi blind SQL injection menggunakan teknik out-of-band (OAST)',
    'An application might carry out the same SQL query as the previous example but do it asynchronously. The application continues processing the user\'s request in the original thread, and uses another thread to execute a SQL query using the tracking cookie. The query is still vulnerable to SQL injection, but none of the techniques described so far will work. The application\'s response doesn\'t depend on the query returning any data, a database error occurring, or on the time taken to execute the query.' => 'Aplikasi bisa saja menjalankan kueri SQL secara asinkron di thread terpisah sehingga respons HTTP utama langsung dikirim tanpa menunggu hasil, error, maupun jeda waktu kueri. Dalam kasus ini, teknik in-band maupun berbasis waktu tidak mempan meskipun celah SQL injection tetap ada.',
    'In this situation, it is often possible to exploit the blind SQL injection vulnerability by triggering out-of-band network interactions to a system that you control. These can be triggered based on an injected condition to infer information one piece at a time. More usefully, data can be exfiltrated directly within the network interaction.' => 'Untuk skenario tersebut, Anda tetap bisa mengeksploitasi blind SQL injection dengan memicu interaksi jaringan out-of-band ke server yang Anda kendalikan, baik untuk menyimpulkan kondisi satu per satu maupun mengirimkan data langsung lewat interaksi jaringan tersebut.',
    'A variety of network protocols can be used for this purpose, but typically the most effective is DNS (domain name service). Many production networks allow free egress of DNS queries, because they\'re essential for the normal operation of production systems.' => 'Banyak protokol jaringan bisa dipakai, namun yang paling efektif umumnya adalah DNS. Sebagian besar jaringan produksi mengizinkan trafik DNS keluar karena diperlukan untuk operasional sistem.',
    'The easiest and most reliable tool for using out-of-band techniques is [[A0]]Burp Collaborator[[/A0]]. This is a server that provides custom implementations of various network services, including DNS. It allows you to detect when network interactions occur as a result of sending individual payloads to a vulnerable application. Burp Suite Professional includes a built-in client that\'s configured to work with Burp Collaborator right out of the box. For more information, see the documentation for [[A1]]Burp Collaborator[[/A1]].' => 'Salah satu server pengumpul callback paling praktis untuk teknik out-of-band adalah [[A0]]Burp Collaborator[[/A0]] atau layanan interactsh serupa yang menyediakan DNS dan layanan jaringan khusus untuk mencatat interaksi saat payload dieksekusi oleh aplikasi target.',
    'The techniques for triggering a DNS query are specific to the type of database being used. For example, the following input on Microsoft SQL Server can be used to cause a DNS lookup on a specified domain:' => 'Teknik memicu permintaan DNS bergantung pada jenis database yang dipakai. Contohnya pada Microsoft SQL Server, input berikut memicu lookup DNS ke domain tertentu:',
    'This causes the database to perform a lookup for the following domain:' => 'Perintah ini memaksa server database melakukan lookup terhadap domain berikut:',
    'You can use [[A0]]Burp Collaborator[[/A0]] to generate a unique subdomain and poll the Collaborator server to confirm when any DNS lookups occur.' => 'Anda dapat membuat subdomain unik pada server callback lalu memeriksa lognya untuk memastikan apakah lookup DNS benar-benar terjadi.',
    'Having confirmed a way to trigger out-of-band interactions, you can then use the out-of-band channel to exfiltrate data from the vulnerable application. For example:' => 'Setelah jalur interaksi out-of-band terkonfirmasi, kanal tersebut dapat dipakai untuk mengeksfiltrasi data langsung dari database target, misalnya:',
    'This input reads the password for the [[C0]] user, appends a unique Collaborator subdomain, and triggers a DNS lookup. This lookup allows you to view the captured password:' => 'Input tersebut membaca kata sandi akun [[C0]], menempelkannya sebagai awalan subdomain callback, lalu memicu lookup DNS sehingga kata sandi langsung terlihat di log permintaan masuk:',
    'Out-of-band (OAST) techniques are a powerful way to detect and exploit blind SQL injection, due to the high chance of success and the ability to directly exfiltrate data within the out-of-band channel. For this reason, OAST techniques are often preferable even in situations where other techniques for blind exploitation do work.' => 'Teknik out-of-band (OAST) sangat efektif untuk mendeteksi sekaligus mengeksploitasi blind SQL injection karena tingkat keberhasilannya tinggi dan data bisa diekstrak langsung, bahkan kerap dipilih saat teknik lain sebenarnya masih memungkinkan.',
    'There are various ways of triggering out-of-band interactions, and different techniques apply on different types of database. For more details, see the [[A0]]SQL injection cheat sheet[[/A0]].' => 'Ada banyak cara memicu interaksi out-of-band sesuai jenis databasenya. Lihat [[A0]]contekan SQL injection[[/A0]] untuk contoh tiap platform.',
    'How to prevent blind SQL injection attacks?' => 'Bagaimana cara mencegah serangan blind SQL injection?',
    'Although the techniques needed to find and exploit blind SQL injection vulnerabilities are different and more sophisticated than for regular SQL injection, the measures needed to prevent SQL injection are the same.' => 'Meskipun deteksi dan eksploitasi blind SQL injection membutuhkan teknik lebih rumit dibanding SQL injection biasa, langkah pencegahannya tetap sama persis.',
    'As with regular SQL injection, blind SQL injection attacks can be prevented through the careful use of parameterized queries, which ensure that user input cannot interfere with the structure of the intended SQL query.' => 'Seperti pada SQL injection reguler, serangan blind SQL injection dicegah dengan menerapkan parameterized queries secara konsisten agar input pengguna tidak pernah memengaruhi struktur kueri SQL.',
    'Find blind SQL injection vulnerabilities using Burp Suite\'s web vulnerability scanner' => 'Menemukan kerentanan blind SQL injection dengan pemindai kerentanan web',
    'If you\'re familiar with the basic concepts behind SQLi vulnerabilities and want to practice exploiting them on some realistic, deliberately vulnerable targets, you can access labs in this topic from the link below.' => 'Jika Anda sudah memahami konsep dasar SQL injection dan ingin berlatih mengeksploitasinya pada target simulasi yang sengaja dibuat rentan, akses seluruh lab pada topik ini melalui tautan di bawah.',

    // cheat-sheet
    'This SQL injection cheat sheet contains examples of useful syntax that you can use to perform a variety of tasks that often arise when performing SQL injection attacks.' => 'Contekan SQL injection ini merangkum contoh sintaks praktis untuk berbagai kebutuhan yang sering dijumpai saat menguji maupun mengeksploitasi SQL injection.',
    'String concatenation' => 'Penggabungan string (concatenation)',
    'You can concatenate together multiple strings to make a single string.' => 'Anda dapat menggabungkan beberapa potongan string menjadi satu string utuh.',
    '[[C0]] [Note the space between the two strings]<br> [[C1]]<br>' => '[[C0]] [Perhatikan spasi di antara kedua string]<br> [[C1]]<br>',
    'Substring' => 'Substring',
    'You can extract part of a string, from a specified offset with a specified length. Note that the offset index is 1-based. Each of the following expressions will return the string [[C0]].' => 'Anda dapat mengambil sebagian string dari posisi dan panjang tertentu (indeks dimulai dari 1). Setiap ekspresi di bawah ini menghasilkan string [[C0]].',
    'Comments' => 'Komentar',
    'You can use comments to truncate a query and remove the portion of the original query that follows your input.' => 'Komentar dipakai untuk memotong kueri dan menonaktifkan sisa kueri asal setelah titik input.',
    '[[C0]]<br> [[C1]] [Note the space after the double dash]<br> [[C2]]' => '[[C0]]<br> [[C1]] [Perhatikan spasi setelah dua tanda hubung]<br> [[C2]]',
    'Bypassing filters' => 'Melewati filter',
    'If an application blocks specific keywords or characters, you may still be able to inject SQL using the following techniques. Encoding-based bypasses, such as URL-encoding keywords or using [[C0]] to construct strings, are covered separately in [[A0]]Obfuscating attacks using encodings[[/A0]].' => 'Jika aplikasi memblokir kata kunci atau karakter tertentu, teknik penyamaran berikut masih dapat diuji. Teknik berbasis encoding seperti URL-encoding atau fungsi [[C0]] dibahas terpisah di [[A0]]Menyamarkan serangan menggunakan encoding[[/A0]].',
    'SQL keywords are not case-sensitive, so you can vary the case of your input to bypass a filter that blocks a specific keyword. For example, if [[C0]] is blocked, try [[C1]].' => 'Kata kunci SQL tidak peka huruf besar-kecil, sehingga Anda bisa memvariasikan kapitalisasi seperti menulis [[C1]] apabila [[C0]] diblokir.',
    'You can also use inline comments in place of whitespace, so that a filter looking for a keyword surrounded by spaces does not match. For example, [[C0]].' => 'Anda juga dapat memakai komentar inline sebagai pengganti spasi untuk mengecoh filter pencocokan spasi, misalnya [[C0]].',
    'On MySQL, you can use versioned comments to hide a keyword from a filter while still having the database execute it. The database runs the contents of a [[C0]] comment, so [[C1]] is treated as [[C2]].' => 'Di MySQL, komentar berversi seperti [[C0]] menyembunyikan kata kunci dari filter sambil tetap dieksekusi database, sehingga [[C1]] diperlakukan sama dengan [[C2]].',
    'Database version' => 'Versi database',
    'You can query the database to determine its type and version. This information is useful when formulating more complicated attacks.' => 'Anda bisa membaca tipe serta versi database untuk membantu menyusun payload eksploitasi lanjutan.',
    'Database contents' => 'Isi database',
    'You can list the tables that exist in the database, and the columns that those tables contain.' => 'Anda dapat mendaftar semua tabel di dalam database beserta kolomnya.',
    'Conditional errors' => 'Error bersyarat',
    'You can test a single boolean condition and trigger a database error if the condition is true.' => 'Anda bisa mengevaluasi satu kondisi boolean dan memicu error database hanya bila kondisi tersebut benar.',
    'Extracting data via visible error messages' => 'Mengekstrak data lewat pesan error terlihat',
    'You can potentially elicit error messages that leak sensitive data returned by your malicious query.' => 'Anda dapat memancing pesan error yang membocorkan data sensitif hasil kueri sisipan.',
    'Batched (or stacked) queries' => 'Kueri beruntun (batched / stacked queries)',
    'You can use batched queries to execute multiple queries in succession. Note that while the subsequent queries are executed, the results are not returned to the application. Hence this technique is primarily of use in relation to blind vulnerabilities where you can use a second query to trigger a DNS lookup, conditional error, or time delay.' => 'Kueri beruntun memungkinkan beberapa perintah dieksekusi berurutan. Hasil kueri lanjutan tidak dikembalikan ke aplikasi, sehingga teknik ini terutama berguna pada kasus blind untuk memicu lookup DNS, error bersyarat, atau jeda waktu.',
    'With MySQL, batched queries typically cannot be used for SQL injection. However, this is occasionally possible if the target application uses certain PHP or Python APIs to communicate with a MySQL database.' => 'Pada MySQL, kueri beruntun umumnya tidak dapat dipakai untuk SQL injection, kecuali jika aplikasi menggunakan API driver PHP atau Python tertentu dengan dukungan multi-statement.',
    'Time delays' => 'Jeda waktu (time delays)',
    'You can cause a time delay in the database when the query is processed. The following will cause an unconditional time delay of 10 seconds.' => 'Perintah berikut memaksa database menunggu tanpa syarat selama 10 detik saat memproses kueri.',
    'Conditional time delays' => 'Jeda waktu bersyarat',
    'You can test a single boolean condition and trigger a time delay if the condition is true.' => 'Anda bisa mengevaluasi kondisi boolean dan memicu jeda waktu hanya saat kondisi bernilai benar.',
    'DNS lookup' => 'Lookup DNS',
    'You can cause the database to perform a DNS lookup to an external domain. To do this, you will need to use [[A0]]Burp Collaborator[[/A0]] to generate a unique Burp Collaborator subdomain that you will use in your attack, and then poll the Collaborator server to confirm that a DNS lookup occurred.' => 'Database dapat dipaksa melakukan lookup DNS ke domain eksternal menggunakan subdomain unik dari [[A0]]server callback OAST[[/A0]] untuk mengonfirmasi terjadinya interaksi DNS keluar.',
    '[[P0]](XXE) vulnerability to trigger a DNS lookup. The vulnerability has been patched but there are many unpatched Oracle installations in existence:[[/P0]] [[C0]] [[P1]]The following technique works on fully patched Oracle installations, but requires elevated privileges:[[/P1]] [[C1]]' => '[[P0]](XXE) vulnerability to trigger a DNS lookup. Celah ini telah ditambal namun masih banyak instalasi Oracle lama yang rentan:[[/P0]] [[C0]] [[P1]]Teknik berikut bekerja pada Oracle versi terbaru, tetapi membutuhkan hak akses tinggi:[[/P1]] [[C1]]',
    '(XXE) vulnerability to trigger a DNS lookup. The vulnerability has been patched but there are many unpatched Oracle installations in existence:' => 'Teknik berikut memanfaatkan celah XXE lama pada Oracle yang belum ditambal untuk memicu lookup DNS:',
    'The following technique works on fully patched Oracle installations, but requires elevated privileges:' => 'Teknik berikut tetap bekerja pada instalasi Oracle yang sudah ditambal penuh, namun membutuhkan hak akses tinggi:',
    'The following techniques work on Windows only:' => 'Teknik berikut hanya bekerja di lingkungan Windows:',
    'The following technique works on Windows only:<br> [[C0]]' => 'Teknik berikut hanya bekerja di lingkungan Windows:<br> [[C0]]',
    'DNS lookup with data exfiltration' => 'Lookup DNS dengan eksfiltrasi data',
    'You can cause the database to perform a DNS lookup to an external domain containing the results of an injected query. To do this, you will need to use [[A0]]Burp Collaborator[[/A0]] to generate a unique Burp Collaborator subdomain that you will use in your attack, and then poll the Collaborator server to retrieve details of any DNS interactions, including the exfiltrated data.' => 'Database juga dapat dipaksa mengirimkan hasil kueri sisipan lewat subdomain DNS menuju [[A0]]server callback OAST[[/A0]] agar nilai datanya langsung terbaca di log DNS.',
];
